WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:16.051
Deployments request a published version for selected devices.
Use a group to update related machines together. A request is
separate from the device installing it and reporting the
outcome. On Devices, open the Device groups tab and create a
group.

2
00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:25.379
Click Manage and add the device to the group. Reuse the demo
group. First-time operators create a group, then use Manage to
add devices.

3
00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.024
In the component library, choose Deploy this version.

4
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:39.168
Select the group as the target. This example also selects
desired state, which keeps this version requested for group
members.

5
00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:47.347
Click Deploy and approve. Device clients process this request
when ready. Creating it alone does not prove installation.

6
00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:03.704
Deployment created. Devices report signed results under
Deployments.

7
00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:14.957
After the Linux device client processes the update, open
Deployments to verify its result. This is a disposable software
test, not a physical Raspberry Pi.

8
00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:30.443
Applied is a verified device receipt: the client downloaded the
software, completed its configured installer and reported
success. It does not prove a long-running service is healthy.
Deployment created alone did not prove this.
